Recommended refined problem statement
Offline-First AI-Powered Healthcare Triage and Emergency Resource Navigation
Millions of people in rural, underserved, and crisis-affected communities face difficulty recognizing the urgency of health and safety situations and identifying the right assistance. This problem becomes even more challenging when internet connectivity is unreliable, healthcare information is fragmented, and nearby resources are difficult to locate.

The challenge is to develop an intelligent, offline-first Progressive Web Application that helps users communicate their concerns through simple, structured interactions; identifies potential urgency using validated decision-support protocols; and guides them toward relevant nearby healthcare facilities, emergency contacts, and local support services.

The solution should support low-connectivity environments, accessible multilingual interaction, locally stored resource directories, privacy-conscious data handling, and reliable escalation to qualified professionals or emergency services when required.

The ultimate objective is to bridge the gap between identifying a possible emergency and reaching appropriate assistance, regardless of continuous internet availability.

